  "issues": [
    {
      "number": 19,
      "id": "I_kwDOQNz9Nc8AAAABOVLQ5g",
      "title": "\"Bytes newly acknowledged during recovery\" might be too vague",
      "url": "https://github.com/kazuho/draft-kazuho-ccwg-rapid-start/issues/19",
      "state": "OPEN",
      "author": "mwelzl",
      "authorAssociation": "NONE",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "The appendix says:\n\n> Under the derivation assumptions, the bytes newly acknowledged during recovery equal one full BDP, i.e., bytes_acked = full_bdp.\n\n\nI would say this is true for the first RTT of recovery. Ideally, recovery shouldn\u2019t take much longer - but it might\u2026 and then this metric might go wrong. Thinking of RACK's way of dealing with recovery by keeping track of the transmission time, I believe that bytes_acked here should be limited to only the bytes acknowledged during recovery whose first transmission timestamp precedes the time of entering recovery.\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-26T11:55:12Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-26T11:55:12Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "comments": []
    }
  ],
